{
  "_readme": "Each line item lists XBRL tags to try IN ORDER, per period; the first tag that has a value for that period wins. 'section': PL (P&L + Quarters, default), BS (balance sheet, annual), CF (cash flow, annual). 'components' = add several items together (each component is its own fallback list). 'optional' = write 0 quietly if the company doesn't report it. 'negate' = flip the sign. 'skip' = write 0 and don't fetch. 'label' must match column A of the Data Sheet exactly. Use 'overrides' to change anything for one ticker. Not sure which tag a company uses? Run:  python fetch_edgar.py TICKER --list-tags word 'ifrs' / 'ifrs_components' = the IFRS tags used for foreign filers that report under IFRS. 'sheet': false = shown on the site but not written into your Excel Data Sheet. 'quiet' = no warning when missing. 'groups' = sum of several optional tag lists with signs.",
  "scale": 1000,
  "items": {
